WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.720
A story that spans decades and even jumps&nbsp;
around in time is bound to have a few plot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.320
holes that could bring the audience's enjoyment to&nbsp;
a screeching halt. However, when it comes to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.680
Fast and Furious franchise, those reality-busting&nbsp;
moments might just be part of the charm.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.240
In the oft-forgotten 2 Fast 2 Furious, Brian&nbsp;
O'Conner finds himself an outlaw living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.880
Miami and doing what he does best —&nbsp;
street racing. The person behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.120
Miami underworld's street racing scene&nbsp;
is mechanic and organizer Tej Parker.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.760
When fans are first introduced to the character,&nbsp;
he's a humble mechanic who used to street race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.320
like Brian. However, after hitting&nbsp;
a wall doing 120 miles per hour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.640
he doesn't drive anymore.&nbsp;
Instead, he just organizes races.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.040
Tej then disappears until Fast 5, when&nbsp;
he's called to Brazil to help Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.640
and Dom Toretto with a heist. That's where he&nbsp;
also demonstrates a renewed ability to drive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.880
an intimate knowledge of high-tech&nbsp;
safes, and the ability to acquire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.800
almost anything in the world for&nbsp;
their odd little safe house in Rio.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.920
By The Fate of the Furious, he's also demonstrated&nbsp;
that he's an expert martial artist and a hacker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.200
that's capable of impressing Ramsey, who multiple&nbsp;
governments are seeking for her technology.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.880
Tej goes from being a humble mechanic to&nbsp;
a world-class criminal mastermind, hacker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.920
driver, fighter, and acquisitions expert.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.560
At no point is the impressive expansion&nbsp;
of his skill set adequately explained.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.640
A brief attempt to justify his skills was made&nbsp;
in Fast 5, but Tej simply said he had a life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.840
before Brian met him in 2 Fast 2 Furious.&nbsp;
That actually muddies the waters further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:46.080
implying he had these skills back then and&nbsp;
chose not to use them. People can get good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.680
at things over the course of their lives, but&nbsp;
Tej is simply too good at too many things.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.760
In Fast and Furious 6, Owen Shaw is introduced&nbsp;
as the man that's been using a team similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.920
Dom's family to conduct all kinds of&nbsp;
unseemly business around the globe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.480
Furthermore, he's recruited Dom's old&nbsp;
childhood flame, Letty, taking advantage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.040
of the fact that the attempt on her life in&nbsp;
Fast and Furious left her with no memory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.400
By the end of the film, Owen is responsible for&nbsp;
the death of Gisele, a member of Dom's crew.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.360
After defeating Owen, Deckard Shaw comes out&nbsp;
of the woodwork to get revenge. He starts by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.320
assassinating Han, a longtime member of&nbsp;
Dominic's crew. He doesn't stop there.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.280
Deckard blows up Dominic's Los Angeles home,&nbsp;
which he shares with his sister, Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.960
and their son. Fortunately, everyone makes&nbsp;
it out alive. Shaw later attacks Dom at Han's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.760
funeral and makes several other attempts on his&nbsp;
life before being captured and thrown in jail.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.760
However, one film later, Dom is backed into&nbsp;
a corner and has no choice but to trust his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:54.240
old enemies with none other than his own baby.&nbsp;
Despite straight-up murdering his close friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.600
stealing his girlfriend and&nbsp;
trying to kill his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.560
Dom trusts the Shaw brothers to not&nbsp;
betray him while they do his dirty work.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.080
Once the mission is over, he&nbsp;
even welcomes Deckard to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:12.720
"family" barbecue in New York City. Forgiveness is&nbsp;
a very complicated thing, but this is a bit much.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.480
The first movie opens with&nbsp;
Brian O'Conner taking his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.080
shot at becoming a detective by going&nbsp;
undercover in the street racing world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.320
The film ends with him befriending Dominic&nbsp;
Toretto and letting him escape custody.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.880
Just like that, he goes on the run and&nbsp;
becomes a full-fledged criminal and fugitive.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.720
He's eventually found by the FBI in&nbsp;
Miami, but instead of arresting him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.240
they recruit him to do a job for&nbsp;
them and bust a worse criminal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.760
He complies with the request,&nbsp;
leading to his record being cleared.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.440
But it doesn't stop there. The next time the&nbsp;
audience sees Brian, he's a full-on FBI agent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:51.760
Now, someone with a clean record can presumably go&nbsp;
through the steps to become an FBI agent. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.040
given that the FBI are the ones that cleared him&nbsp;
in the first place, it's improbable to think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:02.720
they weren't aware of who he was or his propensity&nbsp;
for letting street racer friends escape justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.520
It's almost like the feds get what's coming&nbsp;
to them when Fast and Furious ends with Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.760
predictably, offering to let Dominic off&nbsp;
the hook only to have to orchestrate his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.760
daring prison break weeks later. In the end,&nbsp;
Brian ends up on the "wrong side of a wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.080
poster," but he frankly shouldn't have ever been&nbsp;
trusted on the right side in the first place.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.680
Fate of the Furious had the burden of having&nbsp;
to top the seven movies that came before it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.160
Its attempt to do that can be summed up in a&nbsp;
daring scene in which Dominic Toretto has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.280
face off against his own team in a New York&nbsp;
City chase. Dom, however, has the support of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.560
the criminal mastermind Cipher, who has her&nbsp;
team of expert hackers take over autonomous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:48.720
cars in the city and remotely drive them like&nbsp;
they're a sea of unfriendly metal. Cipher says,

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:54.240
"I want every chip with a zero-day exploit in&nbsp;
a 2-mile radius around that motorcade, now."

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.240
“Hack them all.”

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.160
To put it really, really simply, a "zero-day&nbsp;
exploit" is basically a bit of software that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:08.480
hackers are able to, well, hack. On its own,&nbsp;
it doesn't come anywhere close to explaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:15.040
how minivans and older model sedans could get&nbsp;
"hacked" and driven like remote control vehicles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.680
Simply put, the impressive-looking sea of cars&nbsp;
that Cipher has her team manifest to aid Dom in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:25.040
stealing a nuclear football simply cannot exist.&nbsp;
Not only would the gridlock in New York City be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:30.080
too immense to get the cars past a few miles per&nbsp;
hour, but the scene shows her controlling cars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.200
that the audience is led to believe have both a&nbsp;
cassette player and a high-tech auto driving chip.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.960
The big plot twist in Fate of the&nbsp;
Furious hinges on Dominic's old lover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.560
Elena, having secretly given&nbsp;
birth to his baby. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.360
for those keeping track of the timeline&nbsp;
of events, that really doesn't add up.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.960
Elena is introduced and develops a&nbsp;
romantic relationship with Dominic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.600
in Fast Five. When we see her again in&nbsp;
Fast &amp; Furious 6, she agrees to let Dom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.880
go so he can be with Letty now that she's&nbsp;
alive. Weird, sure, but it's her choice.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.600
To help move on with her life, she joins Lucas&nbsp;
Hobbs at the Diplomatic Security Services.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.080
When we see her again in Furious 7, she's&nbsp;
a full-fledged agent, having clearly gone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:18.560
through whatever presumably lengthy process goes&nbsp;
into making a local Rio police officer who ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:24.080
off with a wanted international fugitive into&nbsp;
a DSS agent. What's more, she doesn't seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.720
be showing a baby bump at all when Deckard Shaw&nbsp;
explodes her and Hobbs out the window of a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.800
tall building. Fortunately, that death-defying&nbsp;
stunt had no impact on her unborn child.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:41.760
Overall, it just doesn't really track&nbsp;
that she would have had a baby with Dom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:48.240
She would’ve had to conceive a child, experience&nbsp;
the events of three movies, and get a new career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.960
off the ground in a matter of weeks. She certainly&nbsp;
wouldn't have been able to hide it from Hobbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:58.480
who would have likely told Dom that he's got&nbsp;
a love child out there. It's a pretty big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.760
plot hole for something that will seemingly&nbsp;
inform a lot of the franchise going forward.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.760
“Everyone meet Brian.”

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.000
Anyone who watched Fast &amp;&nbsp;
Furious 6 was likely struck by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.240
two things during its climax — the&nbsp;
first being the thrilling action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.120
and the second being the fact that it appeared&nbsp;
to take place on a seemingly endless runway.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.080
For those who don't know, the climactic scene&nbsp;
sees the bad guys trying to escape in a plane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.800
with one of the good guys as their hostage.&nbsp;
Dom's crew has to catch up in their cars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.440
somehow find a way to ground the plane and&nbsp;
get their friend off before it takes off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:42.800
What ensues is a roughly 13-minute action sequence&nbsp;
that's truly unlike anything that came before it.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:48.240
Since the movie premiered in 2013, many internet&nbsp;
sleuths and amateur mathematicians have done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:53.280
their best to calculate exactly how long the&nbsp;
runway would have to be in order to accommodate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.720
the lengthy chase. The people at Vulture&nbsp;
factored in the cars' speeds and consulted an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:03.600
actual pilot to tell them how fast a cargo plane&nbsp;
like that needs to go before it can take off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:08.560
and their estimate put the&nbsp;
runway at about 28.8 miles long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.320
The folks at the BBC, however, factored&nbsp;
in the idea that the movie was cutting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:19.040
between multiple things happening at once&nbsp;
and put its estimate at 18.37 miles long.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.400
Regardless, they both agree that the film's runway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:28.480
well exceeds the largest paved runway&nbsp;
in the world, which is around 3.5 miles.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:34.480
Fast and Furious reunited the original&nbsp;
gang from the first movie and is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:40.000
in many ways, the first direct sequel to&nbsp;
the original The Fast and the Furious movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.760
The thing that brings Brian O'Conner&nbsp;
and Dominic Toretto back together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:47.200
is the sudden and tragic death&nbsp;
of their mutual friend, Letty.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.240
When Brian convinced Letty to&nbsp;
be an informant to the FBI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:56.080
she got involved with some bad runners. One of&nbsp;
them, Fenix, betrayed her and chased her down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.760
He wrecked her car and is believed&nbsp;
to have put a bullet in her head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:04.000
Later in the movie, he tells Dom that he&nbsp;
doesn't remember Letty's face. He couldn’t.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.640
"Last time I saw it, it was burning.”

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.840
So, apparently there was a fire.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.760
In Fast &amp; Furious 6, Brian goes to&nbsp;
prison and is told by Fenix's boss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:18.480
that Fenix actually pointed his gun at the&nbsp;
gas tank and blew up the car. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.800
a bullet to the gas tank doesn't always blow up a&nbsp;
car in real life, but that's not the main issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:28.000
The main issue is him saying he definitely&nbsp;
killed Letty and even saw her body burning.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.440
As fans know, Letty was blown clear of the&nbsp;
wreckage. No bullet wounds and definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:38.960
no burns. Instead, she just has a nasty case of&nbsp;
amnesia, which explains why she doesn't remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.280
Gisele bringing her to the hospital where&nbsp;
she was found and recruited by Owen Shaw.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Fate of the Furious begins with Lucas&nbsp;
Hobbs being approached by a fellow DSS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.200
agent to inform him that he needs to recruit&nbsp;
Toretto's team for a job retrieving an EMP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.480
He's told in no uncertain terms that&nbsp;
this operation in Berlin is off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:05.040
books. If he's caught, he will go to prison and be&nbsp;
completely disavowed by his agency. Hobbs accepts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.400
not knowing that Toretto had been approached by&nbsp;
Cipher and blackmailed into betraying his team.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:16.400
Hobbs is arrested and sent to prison, as promised.&nbsp;
However, despite committing a crime in Berlin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:22.800
and being disavowed by the DSS, he finds himself&nbsp;
in a DSS prison, the same one that's housing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:29.280
Deckard Shaw. The question is: If the DSS wanted&nbsp;
to disavow Hobbs for getting pinched in Berlin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.520
why didn't they just let police in Berlin&nbsp;
imprison him? How did he end up in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:38.320
custody of the people that are actively trying&nbsp;
to pretend they have nothing to do with him?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.160
One could argue that Mr. Nobody orchestrated&nbsp;
the whole situation so he could bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.880
Shaw into the mix. However, before Hobbs&nbsp;
actually goes into his prison cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.600
he's approached by Mr. Nobody with an&nbsp;
offer to work for him, which he rejects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.920
This makes the ensuing prison riot&nbsp;
a clear Plan B for Mr. Nobody.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:01.520
Admittedly, no true fan of the franchise&nbsp;
would sacrifice the prison riot scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:05.760
in that movie for all the international&nbsp;
prisoner exchange logistics in the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.800
However, the fact remains&nbsp;
that it's a big plot hole.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.000
At the conclusion of Furious 7, Letty reveals that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.360
at some point during the movie she&nbsp;
got the entirety of her memory back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:20.320
just in time for the news to somehow heal Dom's&nbsp;
wounds and bring him back to consciousness.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.680
By the eighth movie, she's back&nbsp;
to the character we saw last in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:29.120
Fast and Furious. However, it's not fully&nbsp;
explained how Letty got her memory back or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.240
why in the world she decided to sit on that&nbsp;
information until Dom was basically dead.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:38.400
It's very subtly implied earlier in the&nbsp;
film that her fight with Kara in Abu Dhabi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:42.720
may have knocked something loose in her&nbsp;
brain. Sadly, it's never fully explained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.880
and it doesn't look like the remainder of&nbsp;
the franchise has any plans to backtrack to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:51.680
address that. Instead, odds are good they'll&nbsp;
forge ahead with even more reality-bending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.840
over-the-top action movie insanity. Not&nbsp;
that anyone's complaining about that.

